# The vLLM patch series, in the order it must be applied. One directory per
# line, relative to this file; blank lines and '#' comments are ignored.
#
# ORDER IS A DEPENDENCY, NOT A PREFERENCE. Each patch's `file_sha_pre` is the
# `file_sha_post` of the patch before it on the SAME file, so applying them out
# of order is not "still fine, probably" - the second one's pre-image simply
# does not exist yet and `apply` refuses, naming both hashes. Two rules the
# numbering encodes:
#
#   manager.py  0001 -> 0002 -> 0004   (a hash chain: each pre is the previous post)
#   0003 (metadata.py) must precede 0004, which passes the fields 0003 declares
#   on the metadata object as constructor arguments - a semantic dependency the
#   hash chain alone cannot express, because they are different files.
#
# `apply-kvtier-patches.sh` reads this file and walks it in order; it also
# refuses if a numbered patch directory exists here and is NOT listed below (a
# silently-skipped patch is how a half-patched engine happens).
0001-kvtier-pr56810
0002-kvtier-cpu-release-order
0003-kvtier-disk-restore-meta
0004-kvtier-disk-restore
